{
  "abstract": "Pure core Lean 4 (zero Mathlib imports) formalization refuting Conjecture 7.2 of Erickson et al. (JCTA 2025) on standard Young tableau multiset reconstruction for every k >= 8, proving no additive bound n >= k + c holds for multiset reconstruction, proving the universal two-row lower bound N(k) >= N_2(k) >= 3k for every k >= 2, and establishing the pure-kernel lifting framework, k = 3 lower bound for 2 <= n <= 10 and unique n = 14 separation, and k = 4 lower bound for 2 <= n <= 12 (Main results: 8 of 13 in Lean (62%, plus 8 supporting lemmas = 16 compared Lean theorems covering 16 of 21 all proved claims) · 5 by Lean lemmas plus independent computational certificates; zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only). Exact thresholds N(k) for k >= 7 and Conjecture 7.2 at k = 7 on 15 <= n < N(7) remain open. Companion page: https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/syt-hook-conjecture-refutation.",
